  "caption": "Quinn skipped the warm-up, sprinted in minute 12, and the hamstring complained. Quinn blamed bad luck.\n\nHamstrings, ankles, knees and groins are soccer's usual injuries, and structured prevention programs can reduce them. A hamstring strain that keeps coming back often points to unfinished rehab rather than luck.\n\nWhat can help: a structured warm-up such as FIFA 11+ two to three times a week, consistent Nordic hamstring curls, sprinting at training, Copenhagen adductor work for the groin, and managing load spikes rather than playing for several teams at once.\n\nGet checked if you can't put weight on the leg or there's big swelling, and leave the field for any suspected concussion.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
